\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE-1-China's yuan closes outside long-standing range. \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2000\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened to 8.2769 against the U.S. dollar as exporters sold the greenback on Wednesday, closing outside its long-standing band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for the second time in less than a week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which kept the yuan virtually pegged for more than three years. It closed at 8.2775 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Continued sales of dollars by exporters supported the yuan today, but there were no signs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has closed outside its wafer-thin range more than a dozen times since mid-April as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its activity on the Shanghai-based market, China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System. The last time was on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan opened at 8.2771 and hit an intraday low of 8.2778 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  It then rose steadily and moved between 8.2765 and 8.2770, outside the normal band, for most of the session, dealers said. It hit the day's high of 8.2675 due to a single speculative deal, they said. \par \par \uc2  Exports have pushed the yuan higher over the past few weeks. Chinese firms usually export more goods to Western countries in October and November to meet strong demand during the Christmas and New Year seasons. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually settle their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading the yuan with their corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taking advantage of the yuan's strength to test a wider trading range. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan's recent rising tone offers a good opportunity for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test the waters for a wider trading band," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes a harder line when the yuan is soft, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it from closing weaker than 8.2800 to prevent speculation over a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Officials say China is moving towards a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime and studying a wider band to help absorb shocks related to its entry to the World Trade Organisation, which could take place in a few months. They have given no timetable for the move. \par \par \uc2  In a Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts in July, six of 10 respondents said China would allow the yuan to trade in a broader range of at least plus or minus five percent by the end of 2001. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to remain strong in the next few sessions, moving mainly between 8.2765 and 8.2770. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to allow the yuan to move beyond the 8.2770 level. But it was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if appeared ready to end stronger than 8.2764, the highest close since the market was set up in 1994, a record set on May 24. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 7.6340 to 100 yen versus Tuesday's 7.6941. It ended weaker against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0617 from 1.0606. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb802j2b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
