\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends up,flexibility remarks no impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2000\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar on Friday, buoyed by dollar selling from local banks on behalf of exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the market welcomed the renewed pledge by a senior Chinese official that China would move towards greater exchange rate flexibility over time, but it had no impact on the yuan's movements on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2785 to one dollar, compared with 8.2790 on Thursday. It moved in a narrow range of 8.2784 and 8.2791. \par \par \uc2  Turnover fell to $140 million from Thursday's $170 million, according to figures published on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 , the website of the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling from domestic banks on behalf of exporters was the factor pushing the yuan up today," said a local bank dealer. "But there was no impact from official remarks on China's exchange rate flexibility." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Xiang Huaicheng and U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said in a statement after a China-U.S. Joint Economic Committee meeting in Washington that China meeds a more flexible exchange rate to boost its economic development and integration with the world economy. \par \par \uc2  But Xiang also told a news conference it was up to the market, not the government, to determine the right time for making the yuan more easily exchangable. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to enforce the band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for nearly three years on the Shanghai-based national market partly to deter speculation. \par \par \uc2  But it has reduced its activity on the market this year and the yuan has closed outside its band more than a dozen times since mid-April. Officials say China is considering a broader trading band for the yuan but give no timetable. \par \par \uc2  "Bank traders welcomed Xiang's remarks, believing they signalled another pledge that China will relax its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime eventually," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "But they expect flexibility will not occur at least until late next year," he said. "In between, the yuan is unlikely to respond to mere pledges." \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer said the government needed to assess the impact of interest rate liberalisation measures first. \par \par \uc2  It interest rates for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  lending and large deposits above $3.0 million in late September as part of the reforms. \par \par \uc2  "The government typically takes one reform step and waits for its impact before taking another," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has firmed towards the strong end of its normal thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 over the past few weeks, buoyed by increased dollar settlement from local exporters. \par \par \uc2  Chinese trade firms are required to settle most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings with local banks designated to trade on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was expected to move narrowly around current levels in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The yuan strengthened against the Japanese yen to end at 7.4863 to 100 yen from 7.6354 on Thursday. It weakened against the Hong Kong dollar to 1.0606 from 1.0506 but in thin trade. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwar03do4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
