\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends down, dollar rate hike no impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2000\par 07:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 21 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended softer against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, although a 50-basis point increase on some dollar deposits by Chinese banks made no waves in the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan's weakness was not driven by the rate rise because China's rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement system offered few windows for speculation. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down at 8.2780 to one dollar as domestic importers, who are allowed to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from banks only if they provide required documents, sought more dollars for trade settlement, they said. The yuan finished at 8.2774 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  China were allowed to raise interest rates in one-year fixed U.S. dollar deposits of less than $3.0 million to 5.5 percent from five percent from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The rate rise does not affect the yuan's exchange rate because banks do not trade the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to interest rate moves," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Instead, the value of the yuan, convertible only on the current account, is driven mainly by domestic importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after they trade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  "Banks bought more dollars today due to stronger demand from their customers," she said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Beijing's first step towards liberalising its interest rate system would have little short-term impact on the yuan because of the government's tough grip on its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  China requires exporters to sell their foreign earnings to banks and only allows qualified ones to retain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  equivalent to 30 percent of their annual foreign trade turnover. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure could be on the psychological side. The widened interest rate spread may help enhance expectations of a trend of weakening yuan," said an analyst at a foreign bank in Shanghai who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  The one-year fixed deposit rate for yuan is 2.25 percent, compared with 5.5 percent on dollar deposits following the rate increase. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, which has sandwiched the yuan in a meagre trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 for nearly three years. \par \par \uc2  Signs that Chinese exports have been picking up recently have helped push the yuan towards the strong end of its trading band since last week, following two months of weakness. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said, however, the firming could be temporary because China's imports were rising faster than exports and that could put pressure on the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to defend the yuan at the key psychological mark of 8.2800 in the short term to quench speculation of a devaluation, they added. \par \par \uc2  In the long run, China could pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset the impact of membership in the World Trade Organisation, analysts said. China is expected to join the WTO in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan closed weaker at 7.7554 to 100 yen, compared with 7.7426 in the previous session. The yuan gained ground to close at 1.0610 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0615. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9l06trw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
