\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan unchanged, traders flinch at c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2000\par 06:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 29 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed unchanged against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday as bank traders took care not to bid outside the yuan's normal trading band, spooked by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2799 to the dollar, unchanged from Monday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2790 to 8.2801. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept on the sidelines on Tuesday but its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan on Thursday and Monday had sent a strong signal to the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prevent the yuan from breaching the key 8.2800 level. For about three years, the bank had used \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a tool to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a razor-thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  "Bank traders refrained from bidding outside the yuan's normal trading band today as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sent a strong signal to the market," said a local bank dealer. One bid came in at 8.2801, but it quickly stepped back in line. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said strong imports, evidence of recovering economic growth, have kept the yuan hovering around 8.2800, the low end of the trading band, for the past two months. \par \par \uc2  China's latest trade data showed imports surged 40.1 percent year on year to $19.49 billion in July, outpacing a 24.1 percent rise in exports to $21.48 billion in the same period. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account and Chinese banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions after they trade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  Despite the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said the government aim of pursuing a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for entry to the World Trade Organisation was unlikely to change. Beijing expects membership this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said earlier this month the government was considering widening the yuan's trading range, but that it would take time to implement. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move mainly between 8.2790 and 8.2800 in the near term and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible whenever the yuan breached 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  The bank appeared to want to protect the yuan on the weak side of the band to squelch any speculation of a devaluation until a clearer picture of the impact of China's WTO entry on the yuan emerged, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan closed lower at 7.7700 against the yen from 7.6850 on Monday. It finished unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0610. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8t09pa0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
