\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan edges higher on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2000\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan closed a notch higher against the U.S. dollar on Monday after the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan above the key 8.2800 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2799 to the dollar, up from 8.2800 on Friday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2797 to 8.2802. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said strong dollar demand from importers exerted heavy pressure on the yuan, pushing it through the 8.2800 level several times in intraday trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to keep the yuan above 8.2800," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  It was the second time in less than a week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan. "It sends a strong signal to the market that the government is not willing to allow yuan weakness fuel speculation of a devaluation," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the yuan on Thursday. For about three years, the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it in a razor-thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said the government aim of pursuing a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for entry to the World Trade Organisation was unlikely to change. Beijing expects membership this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said earlier this month the government was considering widening the yuan's trading range, but that it would take time to implement. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the yuan breached 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  It would protect the yuan on the weak side of the band to squelch any speculation of a devaluation until a clearer picture of the impact of China's WTO entry on the yuan emerged. \par \par \uc2  Strong imports, evidence of recovering economic growth, have kept the yuan hovering around 8.2800, the low end of its long-standing trading band, for the past two months. \par \par \uc2  China's latest trade data showed imports surged 40.1 percent year on year to $19.49 billion in July, outpacing a 24.1 percent rise in exports to $21.48 billion in the same period. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account and Chinese banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions after they trade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan closed higher at 7.6850 against the yen from 7.7364 on Friday. It finished unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0610. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8s0a0r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
