\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuan weakens,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2000\par 07:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan closed down against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as importer demand soared and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in a month. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2799 to one dollar, down from 8.2796 in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes before the closing bell, which helped the yuan from weakening further. \par \par \uc2  After strengthening briefly at the opening, the yuan spent nearly all the session on a downward slide. \par \par \uc2  It touched a low of 8.2805 in late trade - outside the trading band that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly three years. \par \par \uc2  It reached an intraday high of 8.2790 in between, but dealers said the one tick deal was insignificant. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar buying was so strong that it pushed the yuan all the way down today," said a local bank dealer. "The yuan could probably have ended weaker than the 8.2800 point if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not acted." \par \par \uc2  Minutes before the close, the yuan still hung outside the 8.2800 level, the low end of its long-standing trading range of 8.2770 and 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  very likely stepped in because today's dollar demand was too solid and even got stronger when the market was about to close," said a bank dealer in a foreign bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been hovering around the 8.2800 level, a key psychological support, for nearly two months. Analysts said the weak yuan trend was driven by China's rising imports. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account and Chinese banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions after they trade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  China's latest trade data showed imports surged 40.1 percent year on year to $19.49 billion in July, outpacing a 24.1 percent rise in exports to $21.48 billion in the same period. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said they expected the imports momentum could extend over the third quarter as China's higher-than-expected economic growth of 8.2 percent in the first six months could help stimulate domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen on July 24, did not indicate a change of Beijing's stance to pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for entry to the World Trade Organisation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But this would be a gradual progress and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may intend to protect the yuan to kill any speculation of a devaluation until a clear picture of the impact of China's WTO entry on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan closed down at 7.7262 against the yen from 7.7145. It gained ground against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0618, compared with 1.0620 in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8o0acx9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
