\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan edges higher in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2000\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed up slightly against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Friday as the latest trade data turned most bank dealers cautious. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2796 to the dollar, up from 8.2799 on Thursday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2790 and 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The government said on Wednesday China's imports surged 36.8 percent year on year in July while exports rose 24.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus dropped sharply to $1.99 billion in July from $3.42 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the falling trade surplus would reduce dollar supply on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because the yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  "The July trade data have triggered concerns over the near-term dollar supply on the market," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But the yuan's exchange rates are low after falls in the past few weeks," he said. "Bank traders prefer keeping to the sidelines, waiting for a clear market trend." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said China's falling trade surplus put pressure on the yuan and it was likely to test the key 8.2800 level in the near term. \par \par \uc2  It has stuck to the low end of the usual thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 since early July due to increased dollar demand from importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has long kept the yuan within the thin range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has reduced its activity in the market in the past few months, they said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering a wider trading band for the yuan as China prepares to join the World Trade Organisation, which Beijing expects to happen this year. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan strengthened against the Japanese yen to end at 7.5901 against 7.6248 on Thursday. It closed stronger against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0562 from 1.0605 in thin trade. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8i0as1v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
