\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends lower on trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2000\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 17 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower in thin trade against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as the country's July trade data triggered light dollar buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2799 to the dollar, compared with 8.2791 on Wednesday after moving in a range between 8.2793 and 8.2801. \par \par \uc2  Despite the weakness, dealers said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The government said on Wednesday China's imports surged 36.8 percent year on year in July while exports rose 24.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus dropped sharply to $1.99 billion in July from $3.42 billion a year ago. \par \par \uc2  "July data indicate that China's trade surplus is falling, reducing dollar supply on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a local bank dealer. "This sparked fresh buying in dollars today." \par \par \uc2  Trade is a key factor in deciding dollar supply on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has traded at the low end of its usual thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 since early July as China's imports picked up, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long kept the yuan within the thin range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its activity in the market in the past few months. The bank was last seen supporting the yuan on July 24. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering a wider trading band for the yuan as China prepares to join the World Trade Organisation, which Beijing expects to happen this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said China's falling trade surplus put pressure on the yuan and it was likely to test the key 8.2800 level in the near term. But the potential for a sharp fall was unlikely as exports remained strong. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to stick to sidelines if the yuan drifted marginally outside its usual thin trading range to test a wider trading band. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan weakened against the Japanese yen to end at 7.6248 against 7.5900 on Wednesday. It closed stronger against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0605 from 1.0620. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8h0b49r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
