\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends unchanged, awaits trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2000\par 06:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed unchanged in thin trade on Tuesday as bank traders kept to the sidelines, awaiting China's July trade data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2792 to one dollar, unchanged from Monday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2785 and 8.2795. \par \par \uc2  The government is scheduled to announce July foreign trade data this week. In the first six months of the year, China recorded a trade surplus of $12.3 billion, up sharply from $8.0 billion in the same period of last year. \par \par \uc2  "Most bank traders expect the July trade data to show a continued healthy foreign trade surplus," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "But caution still prevailed in the market." \par \par \uc2  Trade is a key factor deciding dollar supply on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. China's yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move in a narrow range between 8.2790 and 8.2800 ahead of the trade data announcement. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has traded around the low end of its usual thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 since early July as China's imports picked up, dealers said. The central People's Bank of China has long kept the yuan within the thin range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports are also strong, leading to a solid trade surplus which has helped keep a rough balance of dollar supply and demand on the market, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. The bank was last seen supporting the yuan on July 24. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the yuan breached the weak end of its range as the government hoped to minimise speculation about a yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its activity on the market in the past few months. Analysts say the bank is testing the waters for a wider trading band for the yuan as China prepares to join the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan strengthened against the Japanese yen to end at 7.5560 against 7.6062 on Monday. It inched lower against the Hong Kong dollar to 1.0608 from 1.0607. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8f0bapd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
