\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan closes lower, nears weak end of range. \b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2000\par 07:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch lower against the U.S. dollar on Friday on higher dollar demand from importers, which has kept the yuan on a weakening track for the past four weeks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2799, approaching the weaker end of its long standing band of 8.2770 and 8.2800, which the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had enforced for three years through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not act to check the yuan's downward trend on Friday, dealers said. The yuan was down from Thursday's 8.2798 after moving in a range of 8.2788 and 8.2801. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan continued its weakening trend of the past few weeks due to increased dollar demand from domestic importers," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were watching trade closely to see whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be willing to allow yuan to fall through the bottom end of the band. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said last month the government was studying the possibility of widening the yuan's trading band, but gave no timetable. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the yuan could see slight falls again in the near term as there are signs that China's imports are picking up along with the improving economy," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "Whether or not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow the yuan to move outside the usual thin range will be indicative of its attitude towards a wider trading band," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its activity in the market in the past few months, which they viewed as a sign Beijing was moving towards more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed outside the strong end of the range at 8.2770 a dozen times in May and June before the weakening trend set in. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be less inclined to allow the yuan to slip out of the weak end due to concerns it might spark speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Barring \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan was likely to move narrowly around the 8.2800 level in the near term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan weakened to 7.6448 against the Japanese yen from 7.5901 on Thursday. It also ended lower against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0616 from 1.0612. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8400o8k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
