\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends down,importer dollar demand strong. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2000\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 3 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, under pressure from continued dollar demand from importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2798 to the dollar, down from 8.2791 on Wednesday, after moving in a range of 8.2791 and 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan mainly traded at 8.2798 on Thursday, against 8.2790 and 8.2791 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Continued dollar demand from domestic importers kept the yuan weak today," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  In the past four weeks, the yuan settled near 8.2800 - the weaker end of its thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the weakness reflected increased dollar demand as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's imports picked up in recent weeks along with an improvement in national economy. \par \par \uc2  Trade is a key factor in the exchange rate of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, although the yuan was close to the 8.2800 level. \par \par \uc2  "There were no biddings out of the yuan's normal trading band today and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept on the sidelines," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its activity in the market in the past few months, an indication that Beijing might be moving towards more flexible yuan exchange rates. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said last month the government was studying the possibility of widening the yuan's trading band, but gave no timetable. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan's exchange rates were low after recent weakness and the potential for further falls was limited. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move in a narrow range of 8.2790 and 8.2800 in the near term, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan closed higher at 7.5901 against the Japanese yen from 7.7512 on Wednesday. It also ended higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0612 from 1.0620. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw83010lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
