\par\par \b \uc2  China to seek full yuan convertibility - c.banker. \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2000\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, Aug 2 (Reuters) - A top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official will reaffirm China's goal of making its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fully convertible after entry to the World Trade Organisation, according to the text of a speech seen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "After China's entry to the WTO, we will actively create the conditions for promoting the progress of capital account covertibility," said Dai Genyou, director of the monetary policy department of the People's Bank of China. \par \par \uc2  He gave no specific timetable. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now convertible only on the current account, which consists mainly of trade flows. \par \par \uc2  Its international balance of payments was good and the yuan exchange rate was stable, Dai said in the text of a speech to be delivered on Thursday at a conference organised by the International Communications for Management Group. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months, indicating \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already moving toward a more flexible exchange rate regime. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said last month the government was studying the possibility of widening the yuan's trading band. He gave no timetable. \par \par \uc2  But membership of the WTO, which China expects to gain this year, could put pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as imports rise, said Zou Lin, vice director general of the balance of payment department of the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  China could even register a trade deficit, which would put pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and the balance of payments, he said in the text of a speech. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves reached $158.6 billion at the end of June, official figures showed. \par \par \uc2  Dai said the policies of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped the economy record rapid and healthy growth. \par \par \uc2  China's economy is forecast to grow an average seven percent for the next five years beginning in 2001, he said. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product rose 8.2 percent in the first half of this year and grew 7.1 percent for all of 1999. \par \par \uc2  ((Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6586-5566 (Ext. 202). Fax (8610) 8527-5258. beijing.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8200vmp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
