\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan edges higher, trade thin. \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2000\par 06:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 31 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Monday, buoyed late in the session by a spurt of demand for the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from some local banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said trade was rangebound because there was a rough balance of dollar demand and supply on the market. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday high of 8.2790 to one dollar, up from 8.2795 on Friday. It moved in an extremely narrow range for the entire session, touching an intraday low of 8.2794. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan mainly traded at 8.2792 and 8.2793 today," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "It was a temporary need from some domestic banks late in the session that made it close up slightly," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prevent the yuan from straying outside the key 8.2800 psychological level a week ago. \par \par \uc2  For three weeks, the yuan has settled near 8.2800 - the weaker end of its thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan's weakness reflected increased dollar demand as China's imports picked up in recent weeks. But there was also ample dollar supply on the market as the foreign trade surplus has surged this year, they said. \par \par \uc2  Trade is a key factor in the exchange rate of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced its activity on the market in the past few months despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday. \par \par \uc2  They said that did not indicate Beijing would waver in its goal of a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said earlier this month the government was studying the possibility of widening the yuan's trading band but gave no timetable. \par \par \uc2  It was likely to be less flexible in allowing the yuan to push through the weaker side of the band in order to counter fresh speculation of a yuan devaluation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to move in a narrow range of 8.2790 and 8.2800 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan closed higher at 7.5775 against the Japanese yen from 7.6060 on Friday. It ended unchanged at 1.0616 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7v00ymu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
