\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends down in dull trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2000\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened against the U.S. dollar on Friday, under pressure from stronger importer demand for the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2795 to one dollar, down from 8.2791 on Thursday. It moved in a tiny intraday range of 8.2792 to 8.2796, compared with a thin 10-notch band the previous session. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was quiet today. Only some late dollar buying from importers pushed the yuan to close lower," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  For three weeks, the yuan has settled near 8.2800 - the weaker end of its thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This could reflect \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong imports in recent months. Trade is a key factor in the exchange rate of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it did step in on Monday to prevent the yuan from swaying outside the key 8.2800 psychological level. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Monday did not point to a change of Beijing's goal of moving gradually towards a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said last week the government was studying the possibility of widening the yuan's trading band. He gave no timetable. \par \par \uc2  Beijing, however, was likely to be less flexible in allowing the yuan to push through the weaker side of the band in order to quash fresh speculation of a yuan devaluation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan closed down at 7.6060 against the Japanese yen from 7.5200 on Thursday. It ended unchanged at 1.0616 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7s00zep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
