\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Bonds End Mixed; Yuan Flat On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2000\par 12:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government bond prices ended mixed Tuesday as a raft of initial public offerings and a lack of trading incentives continued to pressure fixed-income assets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Three IPOs are scheduled to start their subscription periods this week, siphoning funds away from the bond market, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The bonds are unlikely to move sharply due to the absence of substantial news," said a bond trader in Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended flat at CNY8.2795, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars to importers in the last few minutes of trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened at CNY8.2785 and steadily went up to its intraday high of CNY8.2797 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in. The CNY8.2797 level is near the upper end of the dollar's regular band of CNY8.2770-CNY8.28. \par \par \uc2  "Today's trading isn't a reflection of any future trend. (The dollar's rise) is just due to the normal demand and supply situation," said Fu Qing, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ABN Amro Bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted for foreign-trade purposes and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading is tightly watched by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar rose to CNY1.0618 from CNY1.0615 Monday, while the yen rose to CNY7.7285 per Y100 from Monday's CNY7.7003. \par \par \uc2  With the lack of activities in the government bond market, some traders are shifting their attention to the usually moribund convertible bonds, which represent a small portion of the fixed-income market. \par \par \uc2  The new 10-year floating-rate bond lost CNY0.01 to close at CNY101.91 on volume of 280,297 lots. Its effective annual yield went up to 1.09% from 1.07% Monday. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 eight-year bond gained CNY0.03 to close CNY101.73 on trade of 219,070 lots, with its yield slipping to 3.47% from 3.48%. \par \par \uc2  Market transactions totaled CNY1.25 billion, compared with CNY1.18 billion Monday. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramoncito dela Cruz; Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6248-3268; ramoncito.delacruz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7b03dgj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
