\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan unchanged in sluggish trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2000\par 07:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended unchanged at 8.2776 against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as supply for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  roughly matched demand. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a range of 8.2759 and 8.2777 and dealers said the intraday high could have been a duff quote. There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar supply and demand was more or less balanced today," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Hong Kong's de facto central banker Joseph Yam said China had no plans to allow its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float within a wider trading band in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  Yam said China's central banker Dai Xianglong told him during a telephone conversation on Monday that China would maintain is current yuan policy. \par \par \uc2  "He told me in the short term there was no plan to widen the trading band of the yuan," Yam told television reporters. \par \par \uc2  But Since May 23, the yuan has closed a dozen times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800 in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading over the past month despite the yuan's strength which was backed by healthy trade figures, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Dai's "wider trading range" might be referring to a band that exceeds one percent above or below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate set each morning. \par \par \uc2  "I think what Dai meant a wider band could be a range outside the one percent limit," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  China now caps the yuan's daily trading limit within one percent above or below the price, which is calculated as the weighted average price of the previous trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the limits have barely been tested due to the tightly controlled mechanism of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The narrow 8.2770 to 8.2800 range which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is within the limit of one percent either way. \par \par \uc2  But China was clearly testing the waters for more flexibility in the exchange rate even though it has not scrapped a "managed float" regime, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  China's pending WTO entry has ratcheted up pressure for a more flexible yuan to help absorb shocks to its economy, they say. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers also said that even though the yuan had moved away from its usual wafer-thin band, Dai's remarks could be a sign it would remain stable round current levels for at least this year. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan closed lower at 7.8656 against the Japanese yen from 7.8310. It ended down at 1.0713 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0613. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc