\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends softer on rising importer demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2000\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed several notches lower against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday as importers continued to seek dollars. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2776 to the dollar, compared with 8.2773 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Sometimes dollar demand from importers exceeds supply by exporters and that can push down the yuan," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The yuan, which has strengthened for nearly two months as China posted healthy trade surplus for January-May period, is convertible only on the current account, comprised mainly of trade flows. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the tightly-controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ignored a Hong Kong newspaper report that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) had asked Beijing to float its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as early as the fourth quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  The IMF denied the report after the yuan market closed on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The IMF has not recommended a free float of the renminbi (yuan)," IMF spokesman Jeremy Mark told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, China's Vice Minister of Finance Jin Liqun said he was comfortable with the current managed float \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  "We do not think it is good for the renminbi to fluctuate within too wide a range," he told investors in Japan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Jin's remarks might indicate that China would widen the yuan trading band as an initial step towards full convertibility. \par \par \uc2  "Beijing could face many supervisory risks if it allows the yuan to move too wildly in the immediate future," said a dealer at a major local bank. \par \par \uc2  But China was clearly testing the waters for more flexibility in the exchange rate even though it has not scrapped a "managed float" regime, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually keeps the yuan sandwiched in a slim range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the yuan has closed a dozen times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800 in which the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading over the past month despite the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected market forces would play an increasing role in the yuan market after China joins the World Trade Organisation, expected later this year. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan closed down at 7.8310 against the Japanese yen from 7.8180. It ended higher at 1.0613 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0617. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6r02xw3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
