\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan weakens, unfazed by reports on IMF. \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 07:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed down against the U.S. dollar on Monday, dented by more dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  "More banks bought dollars which their importer clients needed for trade settlement," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2773 to one dollar, compared with 8.2767 on Friday. The tightly-controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unfazed by a Hong Kong newspaper report that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) had asked China to float the yuan as early as the fourth quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese-language Ming Pao newspaper said Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji disclosed the IMF's request to float the yuan either in the last quarter of this year or the first quarter of 2001 to a delegation of top Hong Kong business executives on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and IMF officials in Beijing declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the report could lend further credence to a belief that China is moving towards a more relaxed exchange regime, but analysts said the yuan was unlikely to be floated freely in a short time scle of six to nine months. \par \par \uc2  "I think Beijing is dropping hints that it has more reasons to let the yuan move in a wider range," a dealer at another local bank said. \par \par \uc2  "But a lot more preparation, such as changing market regulations, needs to be done before the yuan could be a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  Said an analyst at a foreign bank: "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the state of development of its financial sector, they're not ready for a freely floating exchange rate yet." \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the yuan has closed a dozen times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800 in which the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a "managed float" for the yuan, usually keeping it sandwiched in a slim range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan is not convertible on the capital account, but dealers said that did not necessarily block a free float under the current account. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said earlier this month China would push ahead gradually with making the yuan convertible on the capital account after entry to the WTO, which is expected later this year. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan closed higher at 7.8180 against the Japanese yen from 8.0501. It ended down at 1.0617 against the Hong Kong dollar against 1.0614. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6q02vlf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
