\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-China declines comment on yuan float report. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Bill Savadove \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, June 26 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on Monday on a newspaper report that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) had asked Beijing to float its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within nine months. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said a free float within such a timeframe was unlikely, but China was already testing the waters for more flexibility in its exchange rate by widening the trading band for the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Chinese-language Ming Pao said Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji disclosed the IMF's suggestion the yuan should be floated in the last quarter of 2000 or the first quarter of 2001 to a delegation of top Hong Kong business executives on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Citing an unnamed source, the daily said Zhu had said he was seriously considering the request and would propose the Hong Kong government submit to him a study on the impact on the territory if the yuan was allowed to float. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the central People's Bank of China said there had been no change of policy on the yuan, which is also known as the renminbi. \par \par \uc2  "The renminbi policy has not changed," he said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF in Beijing was not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  China maintains a "managed float" for the yuan, usually keeping it locked in a tight range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed the yuan to stray outside its usual narrow trading range of 8.2770-8.2800 against the U.S. dollar on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since May ahead of entry to the World Trade Organisation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  YUAN BAND SEEN WIDER \par \par \uc2  Analysts said allowing the yuan to float this year or next could have a negative impact on the financial stability of Hong Kong - a Special Adminstrative Region of China - which pegs its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think they will take much more time to make this free float happen," said Piter de Jong, chief dealer for Germany's Commerzbank in Shanghai. "The only thing they might do is to expand the band a little bit wider." \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the yuan has closed 12 times outside the razor-thin band in which the People's Bank had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself was not ready for a free float, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the state of development of its financial sector, they're not ready for a freely floating exchange rate yet," said a foreign analyst. \par \par \uc2  "In the transition to a floating exchange rate, it has to be accompanied by measures to further develop the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and strengthen the regulatory framework - which is not going to happen in a six-to nine-month time frame." \par \par \uc2  However, both China and the IMF would push for a free float of the yuan in the longer term, analysts said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said earlier this month China would push ahead gradually with making the yuan convertible on the capital account after entry to the WTO, which is expected later this year. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is now convertible on the current account, comprised mainly of trade flows. \par \par \uc2  It closed down at 8.2773 to one dollar on Monday against 8.2767 on Friday as importers bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the market was unfazed by the Ming Pao report. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6q02uro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
