\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan stronger on oversupply of dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2000\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed at its third highest level against the U.S. dollar in six years on Friday due to an oversupply of dollars on the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2767 to one dollar against 8.2771 on Thursday. It was the third highest closing level since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its second highest close at 8.2765 on Monday. It set the record close of 8.2764 on May 24. \par \par \uc2  "There is an oversupply of dollars on the market," said a local bank dealer. "Domestic banks continue to report more demand of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements from exporters." \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened on Tuesday and Wednesday under pressure from dollar demand from importers, but dealers said that demand was offset by an ample supply of dollars. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar supply was underpinned by China's healthy trade performance this year and had supported the yuan's strengthening trend in the past month. \par \par \uc2  China reported a trade surplus of $10.46 billion for the first five months of the year, up from $7.07 billion a year earlier. Trade is key to determining the exchange rate as the yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Since May 23 the yuan has closed 12 times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800 in which the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. Dealers said the yuan has traded mainly between 8.2765 and 8.2770. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, it moved in a narrow range of 8.2766 and 8.2770. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been testing a wider trading range for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. China expects to join the WTO this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could remain strong, but saw near-term resistance at 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended weaker against the Japanese yen at 8.0501 to 100 yen from 7.8660 on Thursday. It was marginally stronger against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0614, up from 1.0615. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6n0311u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
