\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends up amid ample dollar supply. \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 06:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar on Thursday and dealers said an ample supply of dollars on the market helped check a two-day sell-off in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2771 to one dollar against 8.2776 on Wednesday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2768 and 8.2773. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Tuesday and Wednesday under pressure from dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  "There is a surplus of dollars on the market which helped offset demand from importers," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar supply was underpinned by China's healthy trade performance this year. \par \par \uc2  China reported a trade surplus of $10.46 billion for the first five months of the year, up from $7.07 billion a year earlier. Trade is key to determining the exchange rate as the yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Buoyed by strong trade, the yuan has been strong for the past month. On Monday, it hit its second highest close, at 8.2765, since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. \par \par \uc2  The yuan set the record close of 8.2764 on May 24. \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has closed 11 times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800, in which the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading despite the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been testing a wider trading range for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. China expects to join the WTO this year. \par \par \uc2  The yuan spent the past month moving mainly between 8.2765 and 8.2770, dealers said. They said the yuan could remain strong, but saw near-term resistance at 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  It ended down slightly against the Japanese yen at 7.8660 to 100 yen from 7.8404 on Wednesday. It ended higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0615 from 1.0629. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6m0307p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
