\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends lower on importer dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2000\par 06:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 21 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, under pressure from dollar demand from importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2776 to the U.S. dollar against 8.2770 on Tuesday. Despite the weaker close, dealers said the yuan had hovered around the 8.2768-8.2771 level for most of the session. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan kept stable for most of the session," said a local bank dealer. "But it was pushed weaker in the last few minutes of trading as domestic banks bought dollars on behalf of importers." \par \par \uc2  The yuan consolidated on Tuesday. In the previous session, it had hit its second highest closing level since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. \par \par \uc2  The yuan set the record close of 8.2764 on May 24. \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has closed 11 times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800, in which the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading over the past month despite the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been testing a wider trading range for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. China expects to join the WTO this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that given the yuan's recent forays outside its long-standing narrow range, the market had acknowledged a new trading band with a higher ceiling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan spent the past month mainly moving between 8.2765 to 8.2770, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan's strength has been underpinned by China's healthy trade performance. \par \par \uc2  Last week, China reported a trade surplus of $10.46 billion for the first five months of the year compared with $7.07 billion a year earlier. Trade is a key factor affecting the exchange rate as the yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could hold on to its strength, but near-term resistance was seen at 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  It ended down slightly against the Japanese yen at 7.8404 to 100 yen from 7.8203 on Tuesday. It ended lower against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0629 from 1.0612. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6l034zn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
