\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan weakens after second highest close. \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2000\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday after hitting its second highest close since 1994 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2770 to the U.S. dollar against 8.2765 on Monday. Despite the weaker close, dealers said strong demand still supported the yuan and it hovered around the 8.2768-8.2769 level during most of the trading session. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan consolidated slightly today," said a dealer at a local bank. "But the correction is unlikely to reverse its recent firm trend because of a surplus of dollars on the market." \par \par \uc2  On MOnda, the yuan hit its second highest closing level since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. The yuan set the record close of 8.2764 on May 24. \par \par \uc2  Since May 23, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has closed 11 times outside the narrow range of 8.2770 and 8.2800, in which the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept it through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading over the past month despite the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that given the yuan's recent forays outside its long-standing narrow range, the market had acknowleged a new trading band with a higher ceiling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan spent the past month mainly moving between 8.2765 to 8.2770, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has acknowledged the new trading band because of strong supply of dollars," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also seems to have no objection," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is testing a wider trading range for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation, which is expected this year. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been strong for more than a month, underpinned by China's healthy trade performance. \par \par \uc2  Last week, China reported a trade surplus of $10.46 billion for the first five months of the year compared with $7.07 billion a year earlier. Trade is a key factor affecting the exchange rate as the yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could hold on to its strength in the near term, but near-term resistance was seen at 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  It ended up slightly against the Japanese yen at 7.8203 to 100 yen from 7.8800 on Monday. It ended marginally higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0612 from 1.0614. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6k03a06\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
