\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends higher on dollar oversupply. \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2000\par 06:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 19 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed up against the U.S. dollar on Monday on an oversupply of dollars on the market due to China's robust foreign trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday high of 8.2765 to one dollar against 8.2768 on Friday. It touched a low of 8.2770 after a day of dull trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is an oversupply of dollars on the market, keeping the yuan on an upward ride," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan had now risen for more than a month, beefed up by China's growing trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been moving between 8.2765 to 8.2700, outside its normal slim trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 where the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually keeps it by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, the government reported a trade surplus of $10.46 billion for the first five months of 2000 compared with $7.07 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus is a key factor affecting demand and supply of dollars on the market as the yuan is only convertible on current account. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last seen in the market on May 19, had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading over the past month despite the yuan's climb, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was testing a wider trading range for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation, which is expected this year. \par \par \uc2  The yuan set a closing record of 8.2764 on May 24, finishing at its strongest level since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could hold on to its strength in the near term, but gains in the past few weeks would limit its upward momentum. The near-term resistance was seen at 8.2760, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended lower against the Japanese yen at 7.8800 to 100 yen from 7.7683 on Friday. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0614. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6j037hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
