\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan strengthens to end outside normal band. \b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2000\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, ending outside its usual slim trading band for the eighth time since May 23. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2768, outside the normal tight trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually enforces through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bank appears to be testing a wider trading band for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made no public comment on the issue. \par \par \uc2  ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6e03k31\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
