\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-China yuan ends flat, veers outside thin band. \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2000\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Add quotes, background) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 12 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed unchanged against the U.S. dollar on Monday, outside its usual razor-thin trading band for the seventh time within three weeks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2769, just outside the normal tight trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually enforces through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bank appears to be testing a wider trading band for the yuan ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made no public comment on the issue. \par \par \uc2  "Market supply and demand for dollars is roughly balanced today, thus keeping the yuan in a range of only three points," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Trading of the yuan was sandwiched within a tiny window of 8.2769 and 8.2772 on Monday, with most transactions at 8.2771. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan, which has been solid since early May, would remain strong due to China's healthy economic figures. \par \par \uc2  China's exports surged 39 percent year on year in the first four months of 2000. The trade surplus, the key to gauging dollar supply and demand, was $7.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  The government is expected to announce foreign trade data for May this week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yuan trading on May 19. \par \par \uc2  But it has remained on the sidelines since despite unusual movements of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now lcosed outside its band seven times since May 23 and set a closing record of 8.2764 on May 24, finishing at its strongest level since China unified its dual exchange rates in 1994. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the Japanese yen at 7.7302 to 100 yen from 7.7940 on Friday. It also gained ground against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0612, compared with 1.0625 on Friday. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6c03oxt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
