\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends down on importer dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2000\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed weaker against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as domestic banks bought dollars on behalf of importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday low of 8.2780 to one dollar against 8.2771 on Wednesday. It touched an intraday high of 8.2771. \par \par \uc2  "Importers have requested more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from domestic banks recently," said a local bank dealer. "Some banks bought dollars on behalf of importers today, weakening the yuan." \par \par \uc2  Chinese companies cannot trade directly on the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the government requires them to balance their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaps with designated domestic banks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan's close on Thursday was the lowest since May 11. \par \par \uc2  It had strengthened since then, supported by China's healthy foreign trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China posted a trade surplus of $7.3 billion in the first four months of this year and $5.22 billion in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus is key to the yuan rate as it helps decide dollar supply and demand. The yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has closed outside its usually tight range of 8.2770 to 8.2780 five times in the past two weeks without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It set a record closing high of 8.2764 on May 24, ending at its strongest level since China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 1994. \par \par \uc2  Analysts see the unusual movements as an indication the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is testing a broader range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prepare for China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Beijing declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's fall, dealers said the yuan was likely to veer in a narrow band around the present levels because there was a balance of dollar supply and demand on the market. \par \par \uc2  The official Shanghai Securities News said on Thursday turnover on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market surged more than 80 percent year-on-year to $3.168 billion in May. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper gave no details but dealers said the turnover surge reflected China's improving foreign trade this year, which led to more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement from local banks. \par \par \uc2  But the surge had no impact in trading on Thursday as the market had already factored in the news, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China's exports surged 39 percent and imports rose more than 38 percent year-on-year in the first four months of this year. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed lower against the Japanese yen at 7.9505 to 100 yen from 7.7918 on Wednesday. It ended weaker at 1.0630 to the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0614. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6803zed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
