\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan strengthens on trade hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2000\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Wednesday as domestic banks conducted light buying on expectations of strong foreign trade data for May, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday high of 8.2770 to one dollar against 8.2775 on Tuesday. It touched an intraday low of 8.2777 in dull trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The government is expected to announce China's May foreign trade data next week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said domestic banks expected the data to show continued strong exports and a solid trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  "Domestic banks bought some renminbi (yuan) on expectations of strong trade data for May," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  China posted a trade surplus of $7.3 billion in the first four months of this year and $5.22 billion in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Exports and the trade surplus are key to the yuan rate as they help decide dollar supply and demand on the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been strong for a month, supported by China's healthy foreign trade surplus, dealers said. It set a record closing high of 8.2764 on May 24, ending at its strongest level since China unified its dual exchange rates in 1994. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has closed outside its usually rigid range of 8.2770 to 8.2780 five times in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Analysts see the unusual movements as an indication the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is testing a broader range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prepare for China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the People's Bank of China in Beijing declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to move in a narrow range of 8.2770 to 8.2780 in the near term despite the expected strong foreign trade data because it was already at a high level. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed lower against the Japanese yen at 7.7918 to 100 yen from 7.7071 on Tuesday. It ended unchanged at 1.0614 to the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw67045cq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
