\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends little changed, trade thin. \b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2000\par 06:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed almost unchanged against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Tuesday as dollar demand from importers capped the yuan's recent rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday low of 8.2775 to one dollar against 8.2776 on Monday. It touched a high of 8.2771 in dull trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Domestic banks have seen more dollar demand from importers recently and this has helped cap a recent slight upward trend for the yuan," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had strengthened for a month, supported by China's healthy foreign trade surplus, dealers said. It set a record closing high of 8.2764 on May 24, ending at its strongest level since China unified dual exchange rates in 1994. \par \par \uc2  China posted a trade surplus of $7.3 billion in the first four months of this year, up from $5.22 billion in the first quarter, official figures showed. \par \par \uc2  During the recent uptrend, the yuan had closed outside its usually rigid range of 8.2770 to 8.2780 five times in the past two weeks without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the last time the bank was seen in the market was May 19, two trading days before the yuan started to stray out of its thin range. For years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within that band. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the unusual movements in the yuan as an indication the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is testing a broader range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prepare for China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the People's Bank of China in Beijing declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said exports were expected to grow steadily through the summer, which should continue keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the present high levels. But the upside potential was also limited as China's imports were also expected to be strong, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed lower against the Japanese yen at 7.7071 to 100 yen from 7.6730 on Monday. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0614 to HK$1.0. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw66046uo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
