\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Get a bounce from U.S. events. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Richard Hubbard \par \uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2000\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, May 25 (Reuters) - Asian markets enjoyed a \par \par \uc2  welcome bounce on Thursday as dollar longs unwound positions \par \par \uc2  against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and stock investors took heart \par \par \uc2  from a recovery on Wall Street overnight. \par \par \uc2      Even thinly traded Asian benchmark bond issues saw spreads \par \par \uc2  narrow slightly. \par \par \uc2      The better sentiment was driven by the rebound in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq index which posted its first gains after a succession of \par \par \uc2  sharp falls. \par \par \uc2      But sentiment was also boosted by the U.S. House of \par \par \uc2  Representatives decision to vote in favour of permanent normal \par \par \uc2  trade relations (PNTR) with China despite intense lobbying \par \par \uc2  against it by organised labour fearing job losses and expressing \par \par \uc2  concern about human rights. \par \par \uc2  The bill to grant China PNTR status passed by a \par \par \uc2  bigger-than-expected margin of 237 to 197, almost ensuring \par \par \uc2  passage in the U.S. Senate. \par \par \uc2  CHINA ASSET MARKETS MIXED \par \par \uc2  In Chinese asset markets, hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks in Shanghai \par \par \uc2  extended a rally that started last week on the PNTR vote. \par \par \uc2  The Shanghai B share index rose 0.57 percent, or \par \par \uc2  0.266 of a point, to 46.964, back from its midday losses but off \par \par \uc2  a session high of 47.919. \par \par \uc2  The Shenzhen B share index finished one percent, or \par \par \uc2  0.94 of a point, higher at 94.16 on turnover of HK$52.62 \par \par \uc2  million. \par \par \uc2  By Thursday's close, Shanghai's B share market had risen \par \par \uc2  more than 14 percent from May 15 - the Monday ahead of the EU \par \par \uc2  deal - while Shenzhen's B shares were up more than 11 percent. \par \par \uc2  The House vote also cheered domestic A share investors, \par \par \uc2  already bullish after repeated government pledges of support, \par \par \uc2  pushing the Shanghai and Shenzhen bourses through their record \par \par \uc2  closing highs. \par \par \uc2      Shanghai and Shenzhen A shares have gained more than nine \par \par \uc2  percent over the same period. \par \par \uc2      In Hong Kong, the Hang Seng index did jump over two percent \par \par \uc2  in early trade, but all of the gains were erased in the \par \par \uc2  afternoon session as investors went back to selling tech stocks. \par \par \uc2      The Chinese yuan was largely unmoved by the U.S. vote ending \par \par \uc2  lower against the dollar due to technical selling after hitting \par \par \uc2  record highs over the previous two days. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said there were no signs that the People's Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading on Thursday. The \par \par \uc2  yuan hit an intraday high of 8.2766 and a low of 8.2775. \par \par \uc2      SOUTH KOREA SEES ECONOMIC PORBLEMS \par \par \uc2      South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it is a bit worried about \par \par \uc2  the economy, but does not see any kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis looming. \par \par \uc2      The bank's chief Chon Chol Hwan said that while economic \par \par \uc2  conditions have become difficult, he does not expect a repeat of \par \par \uc2  the 1997 \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  debacle. \par \par \uc2      He also predicted GDP growth of seven to eight percent this \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      On bonds, Chon said long term bond yields are being pushed \par \par \uc2  up due to pressures in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and rising oil prices. \par \par \uc2      But he said government efforts to enhance market liquidity \par \par \uc2  would avert any sharp rise in yields. \par \par \uc2      Korean bond prices edged higher on Chon's remarks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  1041 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.42\tab  107.20\tab    -0.20\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7327\tab  1.7355\tab    +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr     30.81\tab   30.82\tab    +0.05\par  Korean won   1129.80\tab 1133.00\tab    +0.28\par  Baht\tab      39.05\tab   39.31\tab    +0.67\par  Peso\tab      42.90\tab   42.85\tab    -0.12\par  Rupiah\tab  8430.00\tab 8495.00\tab    +0.77\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.42\tab  102.21\tab    -4.85\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7327\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.96\par  Taiwan dlr     30.81\tab   31.38\tab    +1.85\par  Korean won   1129.80\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.46\par  Baht\tab      39.05\tab   37.45\tab    -4.10\par  Peso\tab      42.90\tab   40.20\tab    -6.29\par  Rupiah\tab  8430.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -17.26\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  1041 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  16247.82     16044.44\tab    +1.27\par  Hong Kon