\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-UPDATE 1-China yuan back in band, unmoved by PNTR. \b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2000\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In Shanghai story headlined "UPDATE 1-China yuan back in band, unmoved by PNTR" please read in ninth paragraph...The yuan closed at record highs on Tuesday and Wednesday, fuelling speculation...instead of...fuelled by speculation...(corrects to show record highs caused speculation). \par \par \uc2  A corrected repetition follows: \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan was largely unmoved by the U.S. House of Representatives approval of a key China trade bill, ending lower against the dollar on Thursday due to technical selling. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had hit record highs over the past two days. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan closed back inside its regular trading range at 8.2770 to one U.S. dollar on thin volume. On Wednesday it closed at a record high of 8.2764, outside the razor-thin band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally allows it to move. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. House on Wednesday approved a bill that would grant permanent normal trade relations (PNTR) to China. Passage in the Senate is virtually assured by mid-June. \par \par \uc2  The House vote paves the way for China's smooth entry to the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the short-term effect on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was limited as the market had already factored in the PNTR news. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan's movements today were not related to the PNTR partly because the news had been expected," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "Its fall was purely due to technical selling." \par \par \uc2  NO SIGN OF \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading on Thursday. The yuan hit an intraday high of 8.2766 and a low of 8.2775. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at record highs on Tuesday and Wednesday, fuelling speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was testing a wider trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of China's WTO entry. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday marked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest closing level since 1994, when China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 China Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on either day, though the bank normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan in a tight trading band between 8.2770 and 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there would be little downside pressure for the yuan in the near term as China's exports had been strong in the past few months, helping strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan was likely to move narrowly around 8.2770, they said. \par \par \uc2  China's exports rose year-on-year by 39 percent to $72.2 billion in the first four months of this year and the country recorded a strong trade surplus of $7.3 billion in the period. \par \par \uc2  Foreign trade data are key to the yuan's exchange rates because they decide dollar supply and demand on the market. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said China's WTO membership could have an impact on the yuan in the long term. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to come under pressure as China's demand for dollars was likely to pick up on rising imports after it joined the global trade group, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished higher against the Japanese yen at 7.6355 to 100 yen compared with 7.8863 on Wednesday. It inched higher to 1.0615 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0618. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5p03jo3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
