\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends on high, no sign of c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 24 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed higher against the dollar on Wednesday on strong demand by exporters, eclipsing a record close set a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2764 to the U.S. dollar, out of the normal trading band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally keeps the tightly held \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan typically trades in a narrow range of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be testing a wider trading range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the country's entry to the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's close broke the record set on Tuesday, when the yuan finished at 8.2768, then its highest level since China unified its dual exchange rates in 1994. \par \par \uc2  ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4010; Fax 21-6355-5015 reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5o051yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
