\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-China yuan ends on high,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  not seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 24 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed at a record high on Wednesday on strong demand from exporters, beating a peak set a day earlier and fuelling further speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be easing its iron grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2764 to the U.S. dollar, outside the razor-thin band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade. The yuan typically trades in a narrow range of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  The record marks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest level since 1994 when China unified its dual exchange rates and set up the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said on Wednesday there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's close broke the record set on Tuesday, when the yuan finished at 8.2768. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the unusual activity could be a further sign the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be testing a wider range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the country's entry to the World Trade Organisation, which China expects to join this year. \par \par \uc2  "Bank traders seemed more inclined to believe a talk of a test after today's trading as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day despite the record high closes," said an analyst at Bank of China. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  COINCIDENCE? \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials told Reuters in February that the government was considering a gradual widening of yuan's trading band as China pursued its bid to join the WTO. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it was a good time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test a wider band as China's economy was showing signs of improvement and exports were surging. \par \par \uc2  China's exports in the first four months of this year rose 39 percent year-on-year to $72.2 billion, with the country recording a strong trade surplus of $7.3 billion for the period. \par \par \uc2  "There was a possible test by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the widening of the yuan's trading band judging from trading in the past two days," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with a government institution. \par \par \uc2  Any official moves in that direction will be extremely cautious, he said, adding that there had been no official announcements of a test and he did not expect any soon. \par \par \uc2  One dealer at a foreign bank questioned whether the bank really was testing the band as Wednesday's record close appeared to result from a last minute transaction that left the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  little time to react. \par \par \uc2  But speculation is rife with the latest record marking the third time the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has closed outside its band since early April. The yuan slipped through the bottom end of its band on April 12, when it hit a 28-month low of 8.2830. \par \par \uc2  Economists have warned that tariff reductions and the removal of non-tariff barriers that accompany China's WTO membership could cause shocks to the economy and balance of payments, boosting the yuan's role in balancing international payments. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  China's entry to the WTO was imminent after it cleared its last major hurdle on Friday, striking a markets opening deal with the European Union. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say China's pending entry to the WTO should mean more flexibility for the yuan in the near term as the bank prepares for the move. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed on the sidelines, the yuan could test the resistance at the 8.2760 level in the near term. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5o04yj2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
