\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Stocks weaker, pressured by U.S. leads. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 1,140 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 24 (Reuters) - Most Asian stock markets \par \par \uc2  ended in negative terrain on Wednesday despite regaining some \par \par \uc2  ground after early losses on the back of weaker U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2      Losses in U.S. high-tech stocks dragged Tokyo's Nikkei \par \par \uc2  average to its lowest level in a year, with traders warning of \par \par \uc2  more falls to come on shaky sentiment at home and abroad. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets fared better, with regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly off lows. \par \par \uc2      The volatility of U.S. share markets cast doubt on the \par \par \uc2  dollar's ability to attract foreign investment, capping its \par \par \uc2  strength against the yen and the euro. \par \par \uc2      But the yen's strength was tempered by fears that Japan's \par \par \uc2  recovery might not be as strong and broad-based as previously \par \par \uc2  thought. \par \par \uc2      KOREA STOCKS REGAIN COMPOSURE \par \par \uc2      Korea's benchmark KOSPI managed to recoup most of its early \par \par \uc2  losses but still ended weaker after a sell-off in chip making \par \par \uc2  and telecom stocks. \par \par \uc2      The mood was slightly brightened by the IMF's praise for \par \par \uc2  the South Korean economy, saying there was still plenty of \par \par \uc2  "forward momentum". \par \par \uc2      David Coe, senior resident IMF representative for South \par \par \uc2  Korea stressed continued reforms should ensure sustained growth \par \par \uc2  over the medium term. \par \par \uc2      His comments came amid growing worries about a second \par \par \uc2  financial crisis centred on the troubled investment trust \par \par \uc2  industry, the biggest investors in local stocks and bonds. \par \par \uc2      Some analysts joined the IMF in toning down concerns over \par \par \uc2  investment trust companies (ITCs). \par \par \uc2      "I don't think (ITCs) are going to completely impede \par \par \uc2  recovery in Korea. Interest rates will go up as liquidity is \par \par \uc2  strained by these investment trust companies, but only \par \par \uc2  marginally," Bhanu Baweja, regional economist at IDEAglobal.com \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates will come back in the latter part of this \par \par \uc2  year, and the Korean stock market will do better compared to \par \par \uc2  what it's doing right now," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  The won 2 fought back an early slide and was stronger in \par \par \uc2  late trade as players reduced dollars holdings, relieved that a \par \par \uc2  stock market slide was saved. \par \par \uc2  "It seemed that players who raced to build up dollar \par \par \uc2  positions suddenly came to realise Korea's economic \par \par \uc2  fundamentals have not changed much," a foreign bank dealer in \par \par \uc2  Seoul said. \par \par \uc2  CHINESE YUAN HITS HIGH \par \par \uc2  Bucking a glum trend in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the yuan, \par \par \uc2  which closed at a record high on strong demand from exporters. \par \par \uc2  At its highest level since 1994 when China unified its dual \par \par \uc2  exchange rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength fuelled further \par \par \uc2  speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be easing its iron grip. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the unusual activity could be a further sign \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be testing a wider range for the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the country's entry to the World Trade \par \par \uc2  Organisation, expected this year. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment. \par \par \uc2  But they told Reuters in February that the government was \par \par \uc2  considering a gradual widening of the trading band as China \par \par \uc2  pursued its bid to join the WTO. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it was a good time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  test a wider band, as foreign direct investment inflows were \par \par \uc2  healthy and the trade surplus intact. \par \par \uc2  They have warned that tariff reductions and the removal of \par \par \uc2  non-tariff barriers that accompany China's WTO membership could \par \par \uc2  cause shocks to the economy and balance of payments, boosting \par \par \uc2  the yuan's role in balancing international payments. \par \par \uc2  China's entry to the WTO was imminent after it cleared its \par \par \uc2  last major hurdle on Friday, striking a deal with the European \par \par \uc2  Union. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINES HINTS AT RATE HIKE \par \par \uc2  The peso fell sharply, hitting an intra-day low of 42.89 \par \par \uc2  per dollar, prompting the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to say it was \par \par \uc2  seriously considering raising key overnight rates by another 50 \par \par \uc2  basis points. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said rising \par \par \uc2  Moslem insurgency in the southern Mindanao region exacerbated \par \par \uc2  worries in the region over a further possible hike in U.S. \par \par \uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its key rates by a total 125 \par \par \uc2  basis points this month alone in an attempt to stem the peso's \par \par \uc2  decline in the face of political and security worries. \par \par \uc2  "I think there's hardly any reason to buy the Philippine \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  just right now. Everything is pointing southwards," \par \par \uc2  said Baweja of IDEAglobal.com. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the PSB should come in and waste its \par \par \uc2  reserves now," he said, adding that the Philippines should \par \par \uc2  instead concentrate on mending its political risk outlook. \par \par \uc2  Jitters over the peso spilled over to the debt market, with \par \par \uc2  bid rates for Philippine Treasury bills leaping 40 to 50 basis \par \par \uc2  points over their regular auction rates. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was scant demand in the secondary \par \par \uc2  market, amid worries over the potential increase in carrying \par \par \uc2  costs. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0939 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.20\tab  106.53\tab    -0.63\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7355\tab  1.7322\tab    -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    30.824\tab  30.749\tab    -0.24\par  Korean won   1133.00\tab 1134.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      39.31\tab   39.25\tab    -0.15\par  Peso\tab      42.85\tab   42.20\tab    -1.52\par  Rupiah\tab  8495.00\tab 8430.00\tab    -0.77\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.20\tab  102.21\tab    -4.65\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7355\tab  1.6640\tab    -4.12\par