\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan edges up as exports pick up. \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2000\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed slightly higher against the U.S. dollar on Monday, with dealers saying there was an oversupply of dollars on the market as China's exports were picking up. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2770 to one dollar against 8.2772 on Friday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2768 to 8.2773. \par \par \uc2  "There is an oversupply of dollars on the market, keeping the yuan at high levels," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the yuan's upside movements." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But the bank came in to weigh down the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a number of times last week as the yuan was rising on the back of the nation's strong exports and trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China's exports rose a year-on-year 39 percent to $72.2 billion in the first four months of this year and the country recorded a strong trade surplus of $7.3 billion in the period. \par \par \uc2  Foreign trade data are key to the yuan exchange rate as they decide dollar demand and supply on the market. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the tightly controlled market was not affected by last week's agreement with the European Union on China's entry into the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  They said the yuan was expected to hold to high levels this week on a dollar oversupply, but caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to keep it around 8.2770 level. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished lower against the Japanese yen at 7.7270 to 100 yen compared with 7.6100 on Friday. It inched lower to 1.0619 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0615. \par \par \uc2     ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5m00547\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
