\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuans end up,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2000\par 06:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, April 28 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan\tab \tab ended two notches higher against the dollar on Friday, climbing from its intraday low of 8.2805 minutes before the closing bell after apparent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yuan closed at 8.2796 to the U.S. dollar against 8.2798 on Thursday after moving between 8.2795 and 8.2805, compared with 8.2789 to 8.2800 in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Dealers said mounting dollar demand from importers had been gradually pushing down the yuan this week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the central People's Bank of China probably stepped in to support the yuan on Friday after it fell through the 8.2800 mark, a key level the bank usually defends. \par \par \uc2  "A cheap dollar selling order came into the market after the yuan hit the low of 8.2805, and that swiftly lifted the yuan," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "Very likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took action," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the second quarter of each year was generally an active season for imports in China, which led to rising demand for the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  But in the medium term, China's healthy foreign trade balance in recent months might put upward pressure on the yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  China reported a trade surplus of $5.22 billion in the first quarter of this year, up from $4.28 billion in the same period of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended down against the Japanese yen at 7.8344 to 100 yen from 7.8175 on Thursday. It inched up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0626 from 1.0627. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will close from May 1 to 7 to mark the Labour Day holiday. It will be open on Saturday and Sunday. \par \par \uc2       ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab      Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab    Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab \tab  Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab     Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab  Chinese summary\tab \tab \par  Press digests\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4s01jm3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
