\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Rate Hike Lifts Peso \b0\par\par\uc2  By Benjamin Pedley \par \uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2000\par 10:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- A surprise interest rate hike by the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of tighter monetary policy in the U.S. helped the peso higher late Thursday as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended the session mixed. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah rose as fears of political instability after a cabinet reshuffle eased, while the Korean won fell sharply on market fears of a possible liquidity crunch at Hyundai Investment Trust & Securities Co. \par \par \uc2  A day after traders said the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso at an 18-month low of 41.4000 pesos against the dollar, the bank lifted its overnight borrowing rate to 9% from 8.75%. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura expects the U.S. Federal Reserve will lift its short-term interest rates 50 basis points over the next two months. \par \par \uc2  "There is every reason to believe that the U.S. will raise its interest rates...This could have had an impact on the exchange rate and other financial numbers had we not raised ours," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The Fed's monetary policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee meets May 16 and analysts view a 25-basis point boost in the federal funds rate to 6.25% as a near certainty. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the Philippine rate hike was unexpected after indications from Buenaventura and other officials that rates would be stable until after the issue early next month of inflation data for April, and the FOMC meeting. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of trade in Manila, the dollar was at PHP41.260, down from PHP41.310 a day earlier. It made an intraday high Wednesday of PHP41.400. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah rebounded from a six-month low Wednesday of 8,090 rupiah to the dollar as fears of a disintegration of the ruling coalition in the wake of a Cabinet reshuffle eased. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, a meeting of President Abdurrahman Wahid and parliamentary leaders, who were angered by his dismissal Monday of Trade and Industry Minister Yusuf Kalla and Investment Minister Laksamana Sukardi, didn't generate the fireworks that many analysts had expected. \par \par \uc2  Senior leaders of Kalla's Golkar Party and Laksamana's Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle - Wahid's main coalition partners - had raised the prospect of withdrawing from the government, and wanted a full explanation for the firings. \par \par \uc2  But Parliament Speaker and Golkar Chairman Akbar Tanjung said lawmakers didn't threaten to withdraw their support for the president at the meeting. \par \par \uc2  "There was no statement from legislators threatening to pull out support for Gus Dur, although, they are not totally happy with his explanation," Akbar told reporters, referring to Wahid by his Javanese nickname. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at IDR7,930, down from IDR8,023 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Korean won dropped as stock prices fell 3% on worries Hyundai Investment Trust, a unit of Hyundai Group (Q.HGP), may be saddled with bigger-than-expected losses arising from a 1998 takeover of Hannam Investment Trust Co., and a redemption of funds invested in Daewoo Group (Q.DWG) bonds. \par \par \uc2  However, these concerns are unfounded according to Korea Exchange Bank (Q.KEB) - the largest creditor of the Hyundai Group - and South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy. \par \par \uc2  Korea Exchange Bank said Hyundai Group units don't have any financial problems because the group has liquid assets exceeding KRW5 trillion, while a ministry spokesman said Hyundai Motor Co. (Q.HMC), a key component of the sprawling group, will soon announce a foreign strategic alliance. \par \par \uc2  A smaller-than-expected 17.6% rise in South Korea's industrial output in March from a year earlier, and a weaker yen also hurt the won. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at KRW1,110.60, up from KRW1,108.10 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  In Taipei, the New Taiwan dollar ended higher after late \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar ended at NT$30.617, down from NT$30.635 previously,\par and was unchanged late in the Asian trading session against the\par Singapore dollar and Thai baht at S$1.7060 and THB38.095.\par    -By Benjamin Pedley; 65-421-4485; ben.pedley@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4r023eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
