\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady, yen impact muted. \b0\par\par\uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2000\par 03:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 13 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a \par \par \uc2  mixed bag in early Thursday trade, showing little reaction to \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bullishness over Japan's continued recovery and the yen\tab    .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Stock and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were closed in South Korea, for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's general elections, and in Thailand, for the Songkran\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par New Year holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen was slightly off an overnight high of 105.25 though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment remained bright amid growing prospects of a rate hike\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the Bank of Japan (BOJ). The yen was also expected to remain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par well bid due to sustained volatility on Wall Street.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trade was relatively quiet ahead of a G7 summit at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend, during which recent yen strength is likely to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par discussed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     is expected to be range-bound ahead of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy setting meeting later.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Players were also keeping an eye on the Chinese yuan after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it fell to a 28-month low against the dollar on Wednesday, in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par what analysts said could be a test of market reaction to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wider trading band for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Signs of growing dollar demand from importers pushed the yuan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a low of 8.2830 by the close, but traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market by not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Separately, Foreign Trade Minister Shi Guangsheng\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reaffirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stable yuan policy on Wednesday, saying it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had helped Asia's economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In February, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said the government was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par considering a gradual widening of the trading band as China\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pursued its bid to join the World Trade Organisation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of further outflows by foreign equity funds after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wall Street took another beating overnight weighed on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan stocks were 2.6 percent lower at 0137 GMT, battered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by a seven percent drop in the tech-laden Nasdaq\tab     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign equity funds, whose movements have been closely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monitored in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, sold a net T$2.413 billion of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic stocks on Wednesday compared to net buying totalling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par T$946 million on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON\tab     -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was steady in light offshore trade, with domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financial markets shut for the country's 16th general\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elections.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Up to 33 million voters could head to the polls to elect a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new National Assembly. The results are seen having little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact on markets when they re-open amid expectations for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new government to continue with the current reform process.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht was well bid in paper-thin offshore trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Political, business and financial activity is at a near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stand still due to the Songkran New Year holidays on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Monday is also a public holiday though financial markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will be open.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was a shade easier with the slightly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker yen, but players remained wary of pushing it much beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.72, where recent dollar sales by local banks raised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market remained on watch for further merger and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par acquisition activity by local companies abroad, with some talk\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of buying in the baht/Sing dollar cross.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah bandied around levels close to 7,600 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commercially driven trade, as players awaited a Paris Club\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par verdict on the rescheduling of some $2.1 billion worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thursday is the second and last day of Paris Club creditor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meetings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Also eyed were further IMF deadlines for reform, set for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later this week and April 21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was off overnight lows of around 41.21 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early though sentiment remained weak amid lingering political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and economic concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prop up the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts have been pointing to continued jitters over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's ability to manage its balance of payments and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government debt as a driver of further peso weakness, despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positive signals from the IMF and news of a slimmer than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected budget deficit in the first quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Initial peso support was seen at 41.20 per dollar though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels around 42 were seen as a possible target in the medium\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \hi