\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends down on rate rise talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, March 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan\tab \tab ended down against the dollar on Thursday as some institutions bought dollars on expectations China would raise interest rates on dollar deposits following the U.S. rate increase.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yuan ended at 8.2790 to one U.S. dollar, the high end of a range of 8.2777 to 8.2790, against 8.2775 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "Dollar demand increased from early this week. Some institutions might boost positions slightly because of the rate rise," said a dealer at a major local bank. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve raised its key funds rate by 25 basis points to six percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rate rise could point to a possible increase in interest rates for U.S. dollar deposits in China. The one-year deposit rate is now 4.4375 percent. \par \par \uc2  The yuan could see weakness in the near term because of the interest rate pressure and falling foreign direct investment, they said. \par \par \uc2  China's actual foreign direct investment fell 14.25 percent year-on-year in February to $1.854 billion, the International Business Daily reported on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not sit on its hands if the yuan slipped through 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  The yuan also weakened against the Japanese yen to 7.7952 to 100 yen compared with 7.7522 on Wednesday. It ended lower at 1.0635 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0627. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab      Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab    Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab \tab  Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab     Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab  Chinese summary\tab \tab \par  Press digests\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3n03x7d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
