\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends stronger despite Fed rate hike. \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, March 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan\tab \tab closed higher against the dollar on Wednesday despite the U.S. Federal Reserve's overnight hike in interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yuan ended at 8.2775 to one U.S. dollar against 8.2781 on Tuesday after moving in a range of 8.2773 to 8.2786, broader than the 8.2780 to 8.2787 trading range on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The interest rate rise did not affect the tightly controlled market here," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "On the contrary, dollar selling increased slightly as some banks needed to settle for their clients." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve raised its key funds rate by 25 basis points to six percent. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the rate hike could set the stage for a rise in interest rates for U.S. dollar deposits in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There was no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could move if the yuan eased to test 8.2800, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 7.7522 to 100 yen from 7.7604 on Tuesday. It ended higher at 1.0627 against the Hong Kong dollar compared with 1.0637. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab      Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab    Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \t