\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Focus Is On New Taiwan Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 01:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed in early trading Tuesday as market participants wait to see if the New Taiwan dollar would come under additional selling pressure in the wake of the country's presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  Investors shed the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Saturday's election of opposition candidate Chen Shui-bian. Chen's party has espoused formal independence from mainland \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the effects of strong U.S. dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar is scheduled to begin trading Tuesday at 0100 GMT (8 p.m. EST Monday). At the end of trading Monday the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$30.971, up from NT$30.772 at the close of the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar also was expected to be underpinned against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday on expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy making committee would raise short-term U.S. interest rates, although dealers have already largely priced in the hike. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the U.S. dollar was stronger against the Thai baht, but\par lower against the Singapore dollar and Indonesian rupiah.\par - - 21/03/00 00-47G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0040 GMT the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at\par S$1.7182, down from S$1,7189 at Monday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the Indonesian rupiah the dollar was quoted at 7,445 rupiah,\par down from IDR7,453 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said some dollar-selling was occurring after the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was overbought in the wake of the Taiwan elections, helping to lift the\par rupiah and Singapore dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at 38.035 baht, up\par from THB38.005 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won also eased a bit in early trading. The dollar was\par quoted at 1,118.60 won, up from KRW1,118.10 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is slated to open at 0100\par GMT. At the close of trading Monday, the dollar was trading at 40.960\par pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3l01er2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
