\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Baht Rises On Landmark Court Decision \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht strengthened Wednesday after a landmark court ruling boosted market sentiment toward Thailand's economic prospects. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggled to make headway. The New Taiwan dollar came under renewed pressure as fears of an opposition party election victory dented market confidence. The South Korean won's initial gains were erased when the Bank of Japan bought dollars against the yen, lifting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  The baht rose to its highest level so far this month after Thailand's central bankruptcy court ruled that Thai Petrochemical Industry PCL, the country's largest defaulter, insolvent. \par \par \uc2  TPI's creditor banks, which are owed $3.5 billion, had sought the insolvency ruling in the face of opposition from the company's management in what was widely regarded as a test case of Thailand's new bankruptcy law. \par \par \uc2  "This decision is definitely positive for the country's economic prospects," said Kevin Ng, Singapore-based regional economist at ABN Amro Asia. \par \par \uc2  The ruling will strengthen the hand of creditors in debt restructuring negotiations, accelerating the reduction of nonperforming loans, Ng said. High levels of bad loans, at around 39% in January, have been a major deterrent to foreign investment in Thailand, he explained. \par \par \uc2  The court's ruling triggered a flurry of baht purchases, although profit-taking by traders who had previously bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of a favorable decision limited the extent of the rally. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the dollar had been sold down against the baht to THB37.800, below THB37.875 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Given the boost to baht sentiment, dollar offers should cap the market at THB38.000 and drive the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down toward THB37.500 in the short term, said one trader in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar came under pressure as growing expectations of an opposition win in Saturday's presidential election sparked heavy sales of Taiwanese equities Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors emerged as net sellers of local stocks for the first time this month as the Taipei market fretted that a victory for Democratic Progressive Party candidate Chen Shui-bian would lead to sharp deterioration in relations with mainland \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the selling pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, keeping the spot exchange rate tightly range-bound. \par \par \uc2  At the close, the U.S. dollar was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$30.742, little different from NT$30.738 the day before. \par \par \uc2  The won also ended the day little changed after dealers bought dollars to cover short positions following the Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , erasing the won's earlier gains. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the Seoul session, the dollar was at KRW1,118.30, compared with KRW1,118.50 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar lost ground in parallel with the yen, as the U.S. dollar rose to S$1.7106 late in Asia, up from S$1.7071 the previous day. Dealers expected offers to cap the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above S$1.7100. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the dollar closed against the peso at PHP40.930, little changed from PHP40.935 Tuesday. Dealers said corporate dollar inflows coupled with weak corporate demand for the U.S. unit was the main feature in Wednesday's session. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the dollar ended Asian hours at IDR7,441, slightly higher from IDR7,435 the day before in quiet trading ahead of Thursday's public holiday there. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  SUBSCRIBERS CAN FIND ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  COMMENT ON: \par \par \uc2  TELERATE PAGES [1136] OR [4250] \par \par \uc2  DOW JONES NEWSWIRES BY SEARCHING THE CODE N/FXW \par \par \uc2  BLOOMBERG BY ENTERING NI FRX \par \par \uc2  REUTERS BY ENTERING CODE \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /DJ \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3f01d9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
