\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan ends lower on local demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2000\par 04:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 29 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower against the dollar on Tuesday as domestic banks sold the yuan for dollars due to increased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand from importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday low of 8.2793 to one U.S. dollar from 8.2785 on Monday. It touched a high of 8.2785. \par \par \uc2  "We have apparent increased demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from importers in the past two weeks," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "This is an indication that China's imports are picking up after a lull during the Chinese Lunar New Year," which fell in early February this year, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said despite the apparent increase in imports, there were signs that China's exports were also improving. \par \par \uc2  They said they expected China to continue to run a strong foreign trade surplus in the next few months, which would ensure a steady inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  onto the market. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move between 8.2780 and 8.2800 in the near term due to a rough balance of supply and demand of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly-controlled market although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said it planned to widen the yuan's movement range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  An official at the bank said on Friday the government was considering widening the band but had no timetable. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the Japanese yen at 7.4953 to 100 yen compared with 7.5454 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0632 to HK$1.0 from 1.0640. \par \par \uc2      ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn) \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab      Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab    Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab \tab  Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab     Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab  Chinese summary\tab \tab \par  Press digests\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2t067z0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
