\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Mixed; North Asian Mkts Watched \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2000\par 01:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed in early dealing against the U.S. dollar as Asian trading hours begin Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are showing no clear direction, while market attention is focused largely on North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have yet to start trading. \par \par \uc2  Traders and investors are watching the Taipei market carefully after China Monday stepped up its long-running war of words with Taiwan, triggering a sell-off in the New Taiwan dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Although tensions are likely to remain high in the approach to Taiwan's presidential elections on March 18, market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to iron out any volatility and stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to begin at 0100 GMT. At the end of Tuesday's session the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$30.791, up from NT$30.707 the day before. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the won will also be eyed closely after the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped steeply Wednesday. Recent weakness in the Japanese yen, coupled with unexpectedly poor trade figures for January and early February have damped the market's appetite for won risk, leading to heavy liquidation of long won positions in recent days. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, trading in the won is set to start at 0030 GMT. At Tuesday's close the dollar was trading at KRW1,134.00. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, the Thai baht is a touch higher, while the Singapore dollar is slightly weaker. The rupiah is unchanged. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.7070, up from S$1.7060 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB38.155, down from THB38.255 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar is at IDR7,445, unchanged from late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. At the close of trading on the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.680. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2n010le\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
