\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Mixed; Thin Dealing Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1999\par 01:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed against the U.S. dollar as Asian trading hours begin Wednesday, but with dealing almost completely halted now ahead of the New Year holidays, market participants expect few significant moves in the coming session. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. Tuesday EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6656, compared with S$1.6675 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB37.5600, down a touch from THB37.6150 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR7,121, up from IDR7,017 late the previous day. An exceptionally wide bid/offer spread of IDR100 reflects the total illiquidity of the market. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine Dealing System is open for trading Wednesday, with the market closing early at 0400 GMT (11:00 p.m. EST Tuesday). The local market will be closed Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Taipei, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is open for trade Wednesday and Thursday. It will be closed Friday. \par \par \uc2  The outlook for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the new year is generally bullish after the New Taiwan dollar surged to a fresh 25-month high during intraday trading Tuesday in response to positive trade and investment flows. \par \par \uc2  The run-up went largely unchecked by the normally \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raising expectations that the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take a more tolerant stance toward local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  At the close, the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at NT$31.502, a shade higher than its earlier intraday low of NT$31.491, but still well below the previous day's close. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean government was altogether less accommodative of market forces Tuesday, directing large scale dollar-buying by state-run banks, which lifted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the won to close in Seoul at KRW1,142.50. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect state bank buying to continue to support the dollar against the won Wednesday, when the last day of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in Seoul ahead of the new year begins at 0030 GMT. With the local stock market closed, activity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is expected to be thin. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 0228GMT) \par \par \uc2  The Philippine Dealing System is open for trading Wednesday, with the market closing early at 0400 GMT (11:00 p.m. EST Tuesday). The local market will be closed Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Taipei, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is open for trade Wednesday and Thursday. It will be closed Friday. \par \par \uc2  (In an item timed at 0038 GMT, the status of the Taipei and Manila \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was misstated.) \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvct08nge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
