\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Lower; Hits 6 1/2-Month Low \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1999\par 05:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan closed marginally weaker Tuesday in slow dealings, with traders testing the lower end of its trading range. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at CNY8.2793 - the highest level seen since May 26 this year - up slightly from Monday's close at CNY8.2790. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded between CNY8.2789 and CNY8.2793 on trading volume of around $150 million, participants said. \par \par \uc2  "It's noticeable that the yuan is trending lower within the normal range," said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, adding that he didn't see any sign of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Yuan trade against the dollar normally doesn't exceed the CNY8.2770-CNY8.2800 range. \par \par \uc2  Traders still expect the yuan to remain stable in the coming months due to the well balanced capital flows. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is only convertible under the current, or trade account, and trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely regulated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Exporters must sell back 85% of all overseas earnings to state banks. With China's trade surplus of more than $23.8 billion in the first 10 months of the year, the yuan is usually under upward pressure. This forces the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars to maintain the yuan's current level. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Tuesday, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0644 from CNY1.0641 Monday, while the yen ended at CNY8.0351 per 100 yen from Monday's CNY8.0696. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramoncito dela Cruz; (8621)6218-3268; ramoncito.delacruz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc708b5x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
