\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Down As Dollar-Buying Dominates \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 01:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have opened lower against the U.S. dollar as Asian trading hours begin Tuesday, as local corporations' need to acquire dollars to meet month-end debt service obligations continues to dominate trading in a thin market. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar dropped sharply in overnight trading after dollar-buying in New York propelled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up through resistance at S$1.6800, driving the U.S. dollar as high as S$1.6850 early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, profit-taking set in, and brokers in Singapore currently report sizable offers for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from players who were earlier seen going long. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. Monday EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6823, compared with S$1.6765 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at THB39.0800, up from THB39.0350 late the day before. Dealers report steady dollar-buying interest originating in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR7,342, compared with IDR7,320 late the previous day. Indonesian corporate customers are seen still on the bid. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. The peso is generally expected to open lower, tracking the baht. At the close of trading Monday, the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.835. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, trading in the won is set to start at 0030 GMT. Despite government-directed dollar-buying by the state-run banks, most market participants see the won appreciating over the short- to medium-term, supported by favorable trade flows and investment inflows currently running at around $50 million per day. \par \par \uc2  At Monday's close, the dollar was trading at KRW1,159.00. \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to begin at 0100 GMT. Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter any rapid appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen's strength coupled with Taiwan's strong economic performance is likely to attract enough buying interest to push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fresh two-year highs over the course of the coming session. \par \par \uc2  At the end of Monday's session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$31.700. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbu085ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
