\par\par \b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Slightly Lower, But Market Stable \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1999\par 06:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan edged narrowly lower against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, with supply and demand evenly matched. Traders said the market wasn't affected by concerns over a possible yuan depreciation next year. \par \par \uc2  The U.S dollar finished at CNY8.2771, up from CNY8.2769 Monday, trading between CNY8.2769 and CNY8.2772 on deals worth under $100 million. \par \par \uc2  Capital inflows remained strong, traders said, underpinning the yuan early in the session before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased to a softer finish. It wasn't clear if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was active in the market, although traders noted that excessive yuan strength often prompts the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan finished Monday at its strongest point since 1994, buoyed by a hefty trade surplus and rules that require exporters to repatriate 85% of their overseas earnings. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain under pressure in the months ahead. China's exports rose in July after sliding throughout the first half of the year. That export performance lifted the trade surplus for the first seven months of 1999 to over $11 billion. \par \par \uc2  The yuan can be converted under the current, or trade account only. The administrative controls give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  near complete control over the yuan, and taken together with the strong fundamentals, which include about $150 billion in hard reserves, mean speculators can't attack the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  China's government has also pledged not to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. In recent weeks, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have suggested that they may reconsider that promise next year if current fundamentals deteriorate. \par \par \uc2  Those comments aren't affecting the market though, traders said, because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight control over the yuan. "There are only a few transactions done everyday in the market," said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, noting these deals don't accurately reflect wider sentiment toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0664 from Monday's CNY1.0655, while the yen ended at CNY7.2038 per Y100 from the previous CNY7.2278. \par \par \uc2  -By Jason Dean; (8621)6218-3268; jdean@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0456GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8h0637g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
